1
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:08,967
[suspenseful music]

2
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:34,117
NEXT TIME, BE CAREFUL
WHO YOU MESS WITH!

3
00:00:34,201 --> 00:00:37,496
[inaudible dialogue]

4
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:46,797
THIS IS JUST THE BEGINNING,
DON'T YOU FORGET THAT.

5
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:58,100
[inaudible dialogue]

6
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:02,938
[Rob screaming]

7
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:08,902
[henchmen laughing]

8
00:01:15,701 --> 00:01:17,869
[humming] ♪ Cosmic... ♪

9
00:01:17,953 --> 00:01:19,454
[giggles]

10
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:20,747
[in English] We need an extra table.

11
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:22,874
Ah! You can get the side table
in the bedroom.

12
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:24,167
[in Filipino] All right.

13
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:26,670
[Karylle singing] ♪ Cosmic... ♪

14
00:01:28,547 --> 00:01:29,923
[door lock beeps]

15
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,967
[Karylle humming]

16
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:34,720
[Karylle vocalizes]

17
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:36,388
- [knocking on door]
- [vocalizing stops]

18
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:38,890
[tense music]

19
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:40,517
[exhales sharply]

20
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:43,812
Oh? You changed the combination?

21
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,480
Mm... Yeah.

22
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,941
So I have no use for this.

23
00:01:52,154 --> 00:01:54,406
You aren't using the couch I sent?

24
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:55,699
- Uh...
- It's so hot.

25
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:58,243
It doesn't really match
the rest of my stuff.

26
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,288
- That's from France, you know.
- [exhales sharply]

27
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,166
Mama.

28
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:06,585
What are you doing here?

29
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,505
You won't answer my calls or texts.

30
00:02:11,882 --> 00:02:13,925
You blocked me on social media.

31
00:02:14,009 --> 00:02:15,052
What's going on?

32
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:17,137
You know what's going on.

33
00:02:17,804 --> 00:02:20,891
I don't feel like talking about it.

34
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,854
You've been giving me
the cold shoulder for weeks now.

35
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:27,731
Our fans are starting to wonder.

36
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:31,193
[Zsa Zsa] I don't want them to think
there's anything wrong between us.

37
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,321
Isn't there?

38
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:36,406
Let them think what they want.

39
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,242
Don't be ungrateful.

40
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:43,163
The fans and reporters have been
supporting us all these years!

41
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:46,583
They're your fans, Mama, not mine.

42
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,502
And I'm okay!

43
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,003
[Karylle] I'm happy with what I have.

44
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:51,129
You mean to say...

45
00:02:51,922 --> 00:02:54,132
you're happy wasting all your talent?

46
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,968
[Zsa Zsa] And what's all this?

47
00:02:57,052 --> 00:03:00,055
Why not use the studio
that I always use?

48
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,099
Times have changed, Mama.

49
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:03,809
And I'd rather do things my way.

50
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:07,145
When will you prioritize your career?

51
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:09,815
And by "career",
I don't mean those "gigs".

52
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:11,108
You just don't get it.

53
00:03:11,191 --> 00:03:12,818
I love singing!

54
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:14,319
And I love hosting!

55
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:17,364
You're right. I don't get it.

56
00:03:19,074 --> 00:03:22,244
But I want you
to be successful like me.

57
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:29,668
I just don't measure success
by selling out arenas like you.

58
00:03:30,168 --> 00:03:32,587
And I don't need to be a poor copy

59
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,048
of my "Divine Diva" mother.

60
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,226
[suspenseful music]

61
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:47,352
[Rina] Shoot.

62
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:54,443
Andrea...

63
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:02,576
You should have waited for me.

64
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:05,704
How long did you plan this?

65
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:11,251
How deep did you dive into my life

66
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:12,878
so you could hurt me like this?

67
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:14,337
Tell me.

68
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:17,758
[Andrea] No wonder.

69
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,970
No wonder you knew my favorites.

70
00:04:24,139 --> 00:04:26,558
From drinks to food...

71
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:29,561
You even knew
I freaking loved dimsum!

72
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:31,980
It's not what it looks like.

73
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:34,065
Oh, yeah? Tell me what it looks like!

74
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:35,567
It's not like that...

75
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:37,152
What?

76
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,988
You knew everything about me.

77
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:42,115
You were so perfect.

78
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:46,328
And I never saw this coming.

79
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:48,288
Cassie chose you.

80
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:50,957
She picked you over me.

81
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:53,752
- She picked you.
- Wow.

82
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:55,837
Okay.

83
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:58,298
What a soap opera this is!

84
00:04:59,174 --> 00:05:01,551
Nice. What a pitch, tell me more!

85
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:03,220
[shouts] Fine! Okay!

86
00:05:07,349 --> 00:05:10,519
I was going to lead you on,
and then I was going to drop you.

87
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:12,437
Why me?

88
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:15,482
Why me?

89
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:17,025
- [Rina] Babe...
- No, don't!

90
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:18,318
Don't fucking "babe" me.

91
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:19,444
- Please.
- No!

92
00:05:19,528 --> 00:05:20,570
I didn't know I was...

93
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:22,614
- You tricked me!
- Believe me, I love you!

94
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,699
- Oh, my god, leave!
- Babe.

95
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:27,327
- Leave before I hurt you!
- Please, believe me.

96
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:29,621
Oh, my god, just leave! Leave!

97
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:31,998
Leave now!

98
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:33,792
I'm so sorry.

99
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:37,212
- Leave now.
- I promise I...

100
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:40,757
Leave now, Rina.

101
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,218
Please!

102
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,144
[sobs]

103
00:05:57,482 --> 00:06:00,068
[glass shatters]

104
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:03,572
[theme music]

105
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:07,576
♪ Careful, careful ♪

106
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:11,246
♪ The world is full
Of jealous people ♪

107
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:14,749
♪ When envy strikes,
It means trouble♪

108
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:16,960
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

109
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:19,087
♪ Careful, careful ♪

110
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:22,757
♪ We always need to be careful ♪

111
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:26,094
♪ Prying eyes ready to snoop ♪

112
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:29,139
♪ Digging for the juiciest scoop ♪

113
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,766
♪ That's why we need to be careful ♪

114
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:37,230
♪ Careful, careful ♪

115
00:06:39,983 --> 00:06:42,652
[tense music]

116
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:46,448
[air conditioner motor whirring]

117
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:52,495
[lively music]

118
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:08,094
[inaudible dialogue]

119
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:16,144
Thank you, Lord, the AC's fixed.

120
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,979
Perfect. Are they here?

121
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:20,690
Kelly Norman will be late.

122
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:23,026
They're stuck in traffic.
It'll be 45 minutes.

123
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,152
Really?

124
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:26,321
I'm not going to make it to see Joey.

125
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:29,783
Should I see them in your place?

126
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:33,203
A manager needs to sign the contract.

127
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:34,871
Oh, my god. So what do we do?

128
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,708
I need a refill.

129
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:41,544
[Chin sighs]

130
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:42,796
Of course, he won't make it...

131
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,131
What are you on about?

132
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,008
Hollywood is late.

133
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:48,385
Sir Gab can't leave.

134
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,137
So he won't make it to see Joey?

135
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:52,263
Exactly.

136
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:55,558
I have an idea.

137
00:07:55,642 --> 00:07:56,643
[Chin] Huh?

138
00:07:58,353 --> 00:07:59,562
- Is he in there?
- Mm-hm.

139
00:07:59,646 --> 00:08:02,023
[line ringing]

140
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,277
Hello? We need your help.

141
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,780
[in English]
Chin, what do you call this?

142
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:11,282
Oh, that one is called bibingka.

143
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,160
- Oh!
- A rice cake with salted egg in it.

144
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:15,829
- [Kelly] Salted egg?
- [Chin] Yeah!

145
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:19,874
Could you get those notes for me,
the latest from the director?

146
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:22,335
[Kelly] Okay. All right, then. Uh...

147
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:24,212
Gabriel, is there a problem?

148
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:26,506
No, everything's great.

149
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:27,632
Great.

150
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:29,175
I'm sorry I'm late.

151
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:31,845
I'm Matthew Buenaventura.
You must be Kelly.

152
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,555
That's correct! Lovely to meet you!

153
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:35,932
My pleasure!
Kelly, I just need a minute.

154
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:38,143
I need to talk to Gabriel.

155
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,477
- Okay, yeah, sure.
- Okay.

156
00:08:39,561 --> 00:08:40,562
[in Filipino] Let's go.

157
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:42,564
[Kelly in English] Okay.

158
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,774
[Chin] Okay!

159
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:46,443
- Have you tried this one?
- What's going on?

160
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,069
No, I haven't tried that one.

161
00:08:48,153 --> 00:08:49,571
[Matthew in Filipino]
These are Deo's keys.

162
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,489
Take his bike, you can still make it.

163
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:55,452
- Are you sure?
- Just go. Go.

164
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:56,578
[Gab] Thank you!

165
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:11,259
[engine revving]

166
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:18,266
[thrilling music]

167
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:40,205
[engine sputters]

168
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,668
[thrilling music stops]

169
00:09:49,172 --> 00:09:52,467
[heroic music]

170
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,058
[heroic music continues]

171
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,061
[inaudible dialogue]

172
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,065
Drop me off over there.

173
00:10:09,818 --> 00:10:11,152
Okay, this is fine right here.

174
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:12,570
Thank you!

175
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,371
Go ahead.

176
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:26,751
[Gab] I'm sorry.

177
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:29,712
Are you sure I can't go in?

178
00:10:34,551 --> 00:10:36,553
[somber music]

179
00:10:40,515 --> 00:10:41,599
[sighs]

180
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:43,685
Daddy!

181
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:44,811
Joey?

182
00:10:45,103 --> 00:10:46,146
[Gab] Joey!

183
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,064
- [chuckles]
- [relieved sigh]

184
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,526
Gab, you made it!

185
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:53,444
The traffic is horrible.

186
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,071
Are you okay?

187
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,948
Long story, but I'm here.

188
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:58,408
Joey.

189
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,369
Your Auntie Sofie

190
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:05,874
wants you to have this,
so you won't forget her.

191
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:08,751
I'm not forgetful.

192
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,212
You are, Daddy.

193
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,090
Right.

194
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:17,385
I'm the forgetful one.

195
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:20,513
But...

196
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,351
But I promise, this time

197
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:28,271
I'll always think about you.

198
00:11:29,898 --> 00:11:31,149
[in English] You're crying!

199
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,109
[chuckles]

200
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,615
[in Filipino]
You know how to take pictures

201
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:40,158
and videos on your phone, right?

202
00:11:41,868 --> 00:11:46,539
And I taught you how to email,
remember?

203
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,920
So send me stuff every day, okay?

204
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,173
Promise me you'll do that.

205
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:58,218
[Lora] Gab.

206
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:01,346
[whispers] We have to go.

207
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:04,891
[Gab] I love you.

208
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:07,060
[Joey] I love you too, Daddy.

209
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:08,228
[Gab] I love you.

210
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:10,521
[somber music]

211
00:12:11,898 --> 00:12:13,024
Go!

212
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:28,706
Gabriel@shine.com.ph.

213
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,417
[in English]
I will never forget about you.

214
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,545
Canadian English!

215
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:36,256
[in Filipino] Cool!

216
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:37,924
Say bye-bye!

217
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,008
Bye!

218
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:56,276
[cell phone ringing]

219
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,572
- Hello, handsome.
- [Rob over phone] Chin.

220
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:03,199
[crying in pain]

221
00:13:03,283 --> 00:13:04,534
[Rob] Chin.

222
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,620
[tense music]

223
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:08,871
[Chin] Excuse me.

224
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:13,251
[exclaims]
I think that's him over there.

225
00:13:22,302 --> 00:13:26,306
I can't open my eyes, Chin!

226
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:29,058
Can you try walking?

227
00:13:31,394 --> 00:13:32,770
Come on, carefully.

228
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:37,400
[grunts]

229
00:13:39,694 --> 00:13:40,695
[groans]

230
00:13:41,696 --> 00:13:43,614
[groaning continues]

231
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,706
I did you a huge favor.

232
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:54,542
[chuckles] Well, why not?

233
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:56,377
I'm letting you crash here!

234
00:13:56,461 --> 00:13:58,087
[both laugh]

235
00:13:58,171 --> 00:14:01,924
Seriously, cheers to you, Matty.
Thank you for saving me.

236
00:14:02,342 --> 00:14:03,384
And, uh...

237
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:04,969
to Camille!

238
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:07,805
Wow, she's a good kid!

239
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:10,266
Yeah, she's a good kid.

240
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:12,769
To Camille!

241
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:14,896
- To Camille! Cheers!
- [knocking on door]

242
00:14:22,612 --> 00:14:23,613
[Gab] Hey.

243
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:29,077
The first one fucking left me.

244
00:14:29,535 --> 00:14:31,537
And this other jerk

245
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:33,748
catfished me first before leaving me!

246
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:37,460
Why didn't she just stab me
to get it over with quicker?

247
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:38,961
You said you threw her out.

248
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:42,173
Whose side are you on?

249
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:43,591
- I'm clearly the victim here.
- No, I...

250
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:45,134
Right, right.

251
00:14:46,094 --> 00:14:47,387
[knocking on door]

252
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:48,971
Oh! That could be Rina.

253
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:50,348
Smack her one.

254
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,934
[Matthew chuckles]

255
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:55,228
- Hey, Gab...
- Mm!

256
00:14:56,062 --> 00:14:57,355
Looks like we'll need more...

257
00:14:58,689 --> 00:14:59,774
- [Gab] Oh!
- [Andrea] Oh!

258
00:14:59,857 --> 00:15:00,858
...booze.

259
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,946
He wasn't hit in the head

260
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:08,241
but he should get a CT-Scan anyway,
Uncle Matthew.

261
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,953
[Rachel] I can schedule that
when I take my shift at the hospital.

262
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:13,913
Okay.

263
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,081
Thank you, Rachel.

264
00:15:16,124 --> 00:15:17,125
And, uh...

265
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:19,627
not a word to anyone, please.

266
00:15:20,211 --> 00:15:21,587
Absolutely, Uncle Matt.

267
00:15:22,171 --> 00:15:23,214
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

268
00:15:25,842 --> 00:15:26,926
- Here you go.
- [Rob] Thank you.

269
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:31,597
Try not to move too much.

270
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:33,391
You have to rest.

271
00:15:35,268 --> 00:15:36,352
It doesn't hurt anymore.

272
00:15:38,104 --> 00:15:39,814
Even when they were doing it

273
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,900
I was numb.

274
00:15:42,984 --> 00:15:44,819
- Rob...
- Chin.

275
00:15:45,403 --> 00:15:47,405
Rob, you shouldn't have gone there.

276
00:15:47,697 --> 00:15:50,324
Sandra insisted.

277
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,286
She said just one last time.

278
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:57,582
Try to remember everything.
Everything.

279
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:00,084
How can I forget?

280
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:01,836
Uh...

281
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:03,129
I mean

282
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:07,049
for you to tell the cops and lawyers.

283
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:09,051
What?

284
00:16:09,719 --> 00:16:11,804
No. No way.

285
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:13,806
What do you mean "no way"?

286
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:17,477
This is my fault.

287
00:16:17,894 --> 00:16:19,479
[Matthew in English]
Nobody deserves this.

288
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,941
[in Filipino]
No, but it's still my fault.

289
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:27,778
So I just waited for them to finish.

290
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:31,282
As long as they didn't kill me.

291
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,201
Slowly...

292
00:16:33,284 --> 00:16:34,452
I couldn't do that to my Mom.

293
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:35,870
Rob.

294
00:16:37,288 --> 00:16:38,873
Don't be afraid.

295
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,335
He won't get away with this.

296
00:16:42,752 --> 00:16:45,880
We'll protect you.
We'll fight this. Okay?

297
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:46,964
How?

298
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:49,383
[Andrea] What? What do you mean?

299
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:52,595
This is Frank Villacin.

300
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:54,680
[henchmen laughing]

301
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,766
[tense music]

302
00:16:57,308 --> 00:16:59,810
[Rob distant screaming]

303
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:01,187
[Rob] I won't win.

304
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:03,814
[Andrea] Oh, god.

305
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:09,070
Can I go home now?

306
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:16,869
[exhales sharply]

307
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:19,372
[inquisitive music]

308
00:17:22,792 --> 00:17:24,210
[Elisse] You have the luggage?

309
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:25,378
Yes, ma'am.

310
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:29,382
Okay, then this pile and this one.

311
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:31,759
- Okay, ma'am.
- Thank you so much!

312
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:35,304
- Okay...
- [baby toy rattling]

313
00:17:38,641 --> 00:17:41,352
- Andrea, hi!
- [Andrea] Hi!

314
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,396
[Elisse] Thank you! You're here!

315
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:44,522
[Andrea] What's up?

316
00:17:44,605 --> 00:17:48,109
The nanny had to leave urgently,
said there was an emergency.

317
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,194
[lively music]

318
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:59,912
I'm really late for the shoot.
I'm so embarrassed.

319
00:17:59,996 --> 00:18:02,373
Camille will go with you, no worries!

320
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:07,545
No, they're limiting
the people allowed on set.

321
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:09,589
So you need a ride? Let's go!

322
00:18:09,672 --> 00:18:12,717
No, the PM sent
the service car for me.

323
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,843
Oh, so...

324
00:18:15,011 --> 00:18:16,804
[awkward chuckle]

325
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,973
Let me know if you
need anything, okay?

326
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:20,516
[Elisse] Thank you!

327
00:18:25,187 --> 00:18:27,231
I didn't mean to. I beg you, please.

328
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:29,650
I didn't see or hear anything.

329
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:35,990
- [Sofie] Sis...
- Bang! Bang!

330
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,951
Do you know you're useless right now?

331
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:41,621
I was so close! I was feeling it!

332
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:44,248
Come on, I've killed you
so many times today.

333
00:18:44,332 --> 00:18:45,833
You're over-rehearsed.

334
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:47,376
- You're fine.
- But I have to be perfect.

335
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,712
It's my first movie! Noemi, please!

336
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:52,632
Hey, Camille, help me. You do it.

337
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,133
So sorry, Sofie, too busy.

338
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,635
Bang, bang...

339
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:58,387
You do it, Noemi, please. Come on.

340
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,056
Come on. Just one more, I promise.

341
00:19:00,306 --> 00:19:01,682
- Fine, I'll do it.
- [Matthew] Noemi?

342
00:19:01,766 --> 00:19:03,351
[Noemi] Oh! Sir Matthew.

343
00:19:06,312 --> 00:19:07,355
Sorry.

344
00:19:07,438 --> 00:19:09,315
[giggles]

345
00:19:09,649 --> 00:19:10,691
[Noemi] Yes, sir?

346
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,236
Hey, can you help me?

347
00:19:15,071 --> 00:19:16,113
A "bang", that's all. "Bang."

348
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,074
Bang!

349
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:19,950
Hi, guys, Pauline here!

350
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,577
So for today, we're going to be doing

351
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:24,330
some unboxing for some workout gear.

352
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:27,249
A weighted jump rope
that I can play around with.

353
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:30,544
[Pauline] They also sent
a hip resistance band that's pink.

354
00:19:30,628 --> 00:19:33,714
And I'm so excited to use this
in my next training

355
00:19:33,798 --> 00:19:38,052
and I can't wait to show you guys
the next unboxing. Take care.

356
00:19:39,095 --> 00:19:40,388
That's all? That's it?

357
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:42,014
Mm-hm. That's it.

358
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:45,893
[in English]
But that one video will be posted

359
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:48,938
across all of her
social media accounts.

360
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:52,358
Well, doesn't seem like much.
Should we even make an effort?

361
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:53,859
Hm.

362
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:56,529
Definitely.

363
00:20:00,366 --> 00:20:01,742
[Matthew] That's how much
she's getting?

364
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,577
Nope.

365
00:20:03,661 --> 00:20:06,122
This is what SAM is getting from her.

366
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,498
- All that?
- Uh-huh.

367
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:08,958
For 15 seconds?

368
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:10,292
Uh-huh.

369
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,338
Well, not bad!

370
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:15,965
[in Filipino] Let's make some more.

371
00:20:16,132 --> 00:20:17,133
Mm-hm.

372
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,259
[in English] Wait.

373
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:20,886
I have one more question.

374
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:22,763
What is it?

375
00:20:23,264 --> 00:20:24,432
What is "unboxing"?

376
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:26,726
[chuckles]

377
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,940
[Felize crying]

378
00:20:35,276 --> 00:20:37,319
[Camille] What is Ms. Andrea doing
with a baby?

379
00:20:37,403 --> 00:20:39,739
- [Felize crying]
- [Andrea grunts]

380
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:42,116
Okay, who knows how to do this?

381
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:48,748
[Felize wailing]

382
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:50,833
Camille.

383
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,710
- Camille!
- [Camille] Yes, Ms. Andrea.

384
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,295
Bring this all up to my office!

385
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:55,379
Yes, ma'am.

386
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:57,548
Why does it have to be a baby...

387
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,300
[Matthew] It's just one day.

388
00:21:00,718 --> 00:21:02,928
[Gab] I remember
when Joey was this age.

389
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,141
- Andrea...
- Yeah.

390
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:08,476
[in English] Taking care of a baby

391
00:21:08,684 --> 00:21:10,519
is like taking care of your talents.

392
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:12,271
- Really?
- [in Filipino] Yeah!

393
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:14,356
Wait, which talents?

394
00:21:14,607 --> 00:21:16,025
Uh... Maricel.

395
00:21:17,318 --> 00:21:18,736
- [chuckles]
- Monsour-Lav.

396
00:21:20,029 --> 00:21:21,030
[laughs]

397
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,115
What if I do something wrong?

398
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:24,784
[Gab] Then have a meeting with it.

399
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:27,119
That's all there is to it, right?

400
00:21:27,203 --> 00:21:29,038
- You can leave now.
- [boys laughing]

401
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:35,169
- [shouts] Camille!
- [Felize crying]

402
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:36,754
I need a meeting.

403
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,715
[Felize wailing]

404
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,551
When did you learn how to cook?

405
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:44,762
- Have you tasted...
- Bang!

406
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:46,472
Not yet!

407
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:48,265
- Sorry!
- One more line before that.

408
00:21:48,349 --> 00:21:50,017
- Really?
- Yeah.

409
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,520
But you know you can do it.

410
00:21:53,062 --> 00:21:55,147
And Chin will be with you.

411
00:21:55,231 --> 00:21:57,650
No need, I know you're all busy here.

412
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,151
- It's okay!
- No way.

413
00:21:59,235 --> 00:22:01,737
This is your first project
as an actor represented by SAM.

414
00:22:01,821 --> 00:22:03,656
We should document everything.

415
00:22:04,782 --> 00:22:05,950
Okay, one more!

416
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,701
One more? How many does it take?

417
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:08,786
You're good to go!

418
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:09,995
[Sofie] But you just said it!

419
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:12,706
I should always be at my best
and make SAM proud!

420
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:14,917
So one more!

421
00:22:15,292 --> 00:22:17,044
I'm already proud, but okay.

422
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:18,671
- Let me see the script.
- Okay.

423
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:19,922
So I'll know when to come in.

424
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,882
This part! Don't forget.

425
00:22:22,216 --> 00:22:23,217
You forgot this part.

426
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:24,718
- [Gab] This one?
- [Sofie] And one more.

427
00:22:26,554 --> 00:22:27,555
Hey!

428
00:22:35,104 --> 00:22:36,522
Deo!

429
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:38,858
[Sofie] Deo, over here.

430
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:40,609
Can you fix this?

431
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,654
GOSSIP TRIO

432
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:47,992
- So Brandon Vera...
- The MMA fighter?

433
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:50,619
Correct! And his wife Jessica

434
00:22:50,703 --> 00:22:53,998
are rumored to be splitting
and a third party is involved!

435
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:56,792
They've been at odds for a while.

436
00:22:56,876 --> 00:22:58,752
But when we see them in public

437
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:02,423
they're so sweet and touchy-feely.

438
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:05,134
That's called overcompensation!

439
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:08,470
They want to tap out
on their marriage.

440
00:23:08,554 --> 00:23:10,890
Is that really what you want?

441
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:13,392
Well, no one's stopping you!

442
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:16,312
[laughs]

443
00:23:16,687 --> 00:23:19,607
It couldn't have come from our side.
It's almost impossible!

444
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,610
Nobody knows our situation,
not even at home.

445
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:25,613
[over phone]
They never, ever see us fight!

446
00:23:26,739 --> 00:23:28,991
You guys have a lot of employees.

447
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:32,661
[Brandon] I bet you
one of them leaked this story.

448
00:23:32,745 --> 00:23:34,955
Of course they know.
I work with these people.

449
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:39,543
How can they help me keep your secret
if they didn't know the full story?

450
00:23:39,627 --> 00:23:41,545
So the leak really came from you!

451
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:44,757
We won't do that to our own talents.

452
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,508
Let's just ask Ogie Diaz, then!

453
00:23:46,592 --> 00:23:49,470
No! They'll doubt you guys even more.

454
00:23:49,553 --> 00:23:52,139
[Brandon] Hey, you better fix this.

455
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:55,434
I don't want anybody coming after us
for breach of contract.

456
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:56,852
Nobody wants that.

457
00:23:57,353 --> 00:23:58,771
Just keep on doing what you're doing.

458
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:01,607
Please, man.

459
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:03,359
[Matthew over phone] Okay. Stay safe.

460
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:15,663
I never told anyone, Sir Matthew.

461
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:18,082
Everything I know
stays in this office.

462
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,583
I know.

463
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,043
You, I trust.

464
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:22,544
But who's doing this?

465
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,463
I'll try to find out.

466
00:24:24,546 --> 00:24:26,966
I don't know how, but I'll try.

467
00:24:30,386 --> 00:24:32,763
Not everything should be exposed.

468
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:36,809
That's why I'm hiding these cables.

469
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:47,736
[suspenseful music]

470
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:54,785
[doctor] So far, all is well.

471
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,912
Everything looks okay.

472
00:24:57,621 --> 00:24:59,373
And good for you

473
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:01,208
you're not keloidal.

474
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:04,378
Those scabs on your body
will lighten eventually.

475
00:25:04,962 --> 00:25:06,005
- Okay?
- [Rob] Doc...

476
00:25:06,088 --> 00:25:07,089
I feel great!

477
00:25:07,172 --> 00:25:10,300
[doctor] Good, then I guess
you're clear for now!

478
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:13,595
Perfect. Okay, thanks, Doc!

479
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:15,681
Thank you.

480
00:25:20,394 --> 00:25:21,770
[mouths] Okay?

481
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:23,147
[doctor] Nurse Rachel
will see you out.

482
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:24,982
[Rob] Thanks, Doc!

483
00:25:25,232 --> 00:25:27,943
Hey, how about a picture with Rob?

484
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:30,821
- [Chin] Rob, is it okay?
- [nurse] Sir, just one picture.

485
00:25:30,904 --> 00:25:32,197
[Chin] Just a picture.

486
00:25:33,282 --> 00:25:36,368
Okay, one, two, three, smile!

487
00:25:36,869 --> 00:25:38,996
Can you take a picture on mine too?

488
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:41,373
- [Chin] Right away, come on!
- [nurse] Thank you.

489
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:46,045
Okay. One, two, three, smile!

490
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:49,840
- Thank you!
- Thank you! Let's go.

491
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:55,554
- Oh, my god! We want pictures too!
- [Chin] No, sorry...

492
00:25:55,637 --> 00:25:57,139
Sorry, excuse us.

493
00:25:57,222 --> 00:26:00,267
- We have another meeting to go to.
- [woman fan] Just one!

494
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:03,270
Sorry, we're in a rush.

495
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:04,396
We waited for nothing.

496
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,148
[nurse] Sir, excuse me, sir!

497
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:08,150
Excuse me, you left your phone.

498
00:26:08,692 --> 00:26:09,735
- Take care.
- [Chin] Thank you.

499
00:26:21,789 --> 00:26:24,374
How's the Vivamax project going?

500
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:26,251
My siblings are so excited.

501
00:26:26,335 --> 00:26:27,503
Your siblings?

502
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:30,297
[chuckles]
Yeah, we need a new laptop.

503
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:31,673
[Rob] It's an old model.

504
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:33,175
But we used it a lot.

505
00:26:36,512 --> 00:26:38,055
I'm okay, Chin!

506
00:26:42,392 --> 00:26:43,602
Are you sure?

507
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:48,982
Are you sure you don't need
any justice for what happened?

508
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,818
I'm done with all of it.

509
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,445
I'm a changed man.

510
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:58,784
What if, and this is
a huge "what if"...

511
00:26:59,785 --> 00:27:02,913
What if someone else exposes
what Frank Villacin did to you?

512
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:04,373
Chin! Don't do it.

513
00:27:05,999 --> 00:27:07,835
I'm serious.

514
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:09,461
I don't want you involved in this.

515
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:11,004
I said it was a "what if".

516
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:16,468
Where the hell have you been?

517
00:27:17,136 --> 00:27:18,220
The toilet.

518
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,055
Let's go.

519
00:27:20,139 --> 00:27:22,474
[dramatic music]

520
00:27:24,226 --> 00:27:25,686
[Andrea] "Feed every four hours..."

521
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:27,062
"Don't forget to sterilize..."

522
00:27:27,146 --> 00:27:30,107
Now how do I do that
if the sterilizer isn't here?

523
00:27:31,066 --> 00:27:32,109
Okay.

524
00:27:34,987 --> 00:27:36,738
"Check diaper every 30 minutes."

525
00:27:36,822 --> 00:27:39,074
Check diaper every 30 minutes.

526
00:27:41,994 --> 00:27:43,495
How cute!

527
00:27:45,038 --> 00:27:46,874
Post that and you're fired.

528
00:27:46,957 --> 00:27:49,001
- No, I won't.
- [Andrea] Hey, K.

529
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:50,961
- Hi!
- Hi, how are you?

530
00:27:51,044 --> 00:27:52,087
What's up?

531
00:27:52,171 --> 00:27:53,213
Sit!

532
00:27:53,297 --> 00:27:54,339
Hey, baby!

533
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:57,759
We just want to show you
what we've been working on.

534
00:27:57,843 --> 00:27:58,886
- Super exciting!
- Okay.

535
00:27:58,969 --> 00:28:01,346
- It's amazing, Ms. Andrea!
- What's all this?

536
00:28:01,430 --> 00:28:04,808
We posted Karylle's latest songs
on YouTube Music.

537
00:28:04,892 --> 00:28:07,227
We already have so many likes!
She's amazing!

538
00:28:07,311 --> 00:28:08,937
♪ Mix the beat of... ♪

539
00:28:09,021 --> 00:28:10,647
[Andrea] I see you enjoyed
working on this.

540
00:28:10,731 --> 00:28:13,275
It always feels good to make music,
especially if there's no pressure.

541
00:28:13,358 --> 00:28:14,401
This is so much fun!

542
00:28:14,484 --> 00:28:17,404
♪ 'Til everything's
Fine, fine, fine ♪

543
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,449
♪ We crawl and we stop,
We walk and we run ♪

544
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:22,409
[Camille] The posts
are so well-received.

545
00:28:22,492 --> 00:28:25,662
On all her socials,
the reaction is great!

546
00:28:26,288 --> 00:28:27,706
So I made these for her.

547
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:30,083
[Andrea] Mm...

548
00:28:30,167 --> 00:28:31,335
Nice! Good job.

549
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:35,297
Camille, next time, I'd appreciate it
if you let me know beforehand.

550
00:28:35,923 --> 00:28:36,924
Yes, ma'am.

551
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:39,259
I think Matt and Gab
would like to see that as well.

552
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:41,929
Um... But you know,
you're serving it!

553
00:28:42,012 --> 00:28:43,180
- You're serving it.
- [squeals]

554
00:28:43,263 --> 00:28:46,225
She's so creative
and so chill to work with!

555
00:28:46,308 --> 00:28:47,351
Uh-huh.

556
00:28:47,434 --> 00:28:48,518
She's so good at what she does.

557
00:28:48,602 --> 00:28:50,145
Should I call them, or you?

558
00:28:50,229 --> 00:28:52,231
No, I will, of course. Here I go.

559
00:28:52,606 --> 00:28:54,816
Gosh. It's so hot today.

560
00:28:56,276 --> 00:28:58,528
It's sunny outside,
but raining in here?

561
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,614
I know, right?

562
00:29:00,697 --> 00:29:02,908
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

563
00:29:02,991 --> 00:29:03,992
What's that noise?

564
00:29:05,035 --> 00:29:06,536
A meeting, as usual.

565
00:29:06,912 --> 00:29:08,538
Karylle is in there.

566
00:29:08,789 --> 00:29:10,582
They're meeting about her socials.

567
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,251
Everyone?

568
00:29:12,334 --> 00:29:13,752
- Mm-hm.
- [Daisy] Uh-huh.

569
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:16,713
Okay.

570
00:29:17,798 --> 00:29:20,008
Your horns are showing, Satan.

571
00:29:20,509 --> 00:29:21,802
What did I say?

572
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:26,348
What's that?

573
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:27,891
Set cards.

574
00:29:27,975 --> 00:29:30,185
[Daisy] The meeting's over?

575
00:29:30,269 --> 00:29:31,436
- Yes, it just ended.
- Yes.

576
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:35,190
What's the fuss
with Karylle's social media?

577
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:39,861
Glad they liked it,
but Matthew is so funny!

578
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:42,239
He liked and commented
on my page so much

579
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:43,532
that he earned a top fan badge!

580
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:46,576
[Camille] That's why he was asking
about the award he got!

581
00:29:46,660 --> 00:29:48,036
- [Karylle] That's what it was!
- Bye-bye!

582
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:49,663
Bye, take care! Chin!

583
00:29:50,038 --> 00:29:51,248
How's Rob?

584
00:29:51,331 --> 00:29:53,083
Doing much better, why?

585
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:55,294
We missed you at the meeting.

586
00:29:55,377 --> 00:29:57,754
We presented artwork
for Karylle's page.

587
00:29:58,088 --> 00:29:59,715
The bosses were so happy!

588
00:30:00,299 --> 00:30:01,341
Oh, well.

589
00:30:02,092 --> 00:30:03,468
You can still help us!

590
00:30:03,552 --> 00:30:04,970
Maybe you can think of more content.

591
00:30:05,053 --> 00:30:06,305
You're so good at stuff like that.

592
00:30:06,722 --> 00:30:07,764
No worries.

593
00:30:08,098 --> 00:30:09,641
Your dad is in the meeting, right?

594
00:30:09,725 --> 00:30:11,184
I'm sure he helped you a lot!

595
00:30:11,435 --> 00:30:12,477
[Sofie] Chin.

596
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:16,690
Camille.

597
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:20,527
I'll give you access to the apps.

598
00:30:26,116 --> 00:30:27,117
You are so mean.

599
00:30:27,451 --> 00:30:29,453
[indistinct chatter]

600
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:35,667
Camille.

601
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:38,920
[in English] Everybody knows now.

602
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:43,467
[in Filipino]
It would've been okay if they didn't.

603
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:46,053
Maybe you shouldn't have told them.

604
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:49,264
Are Noemi and Chin
giving you a hard time?

605
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:53,226
Maybe they see me differently now.

606
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:54,936
[in English]
Like, I don't know if they trust me.

607
00:30:57,189 --> 00:30:59,232
[in Filipino]
This is RM level office politics.

608
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,069
[in English] Well, I trust you.

609
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:06,031
Matt?

610
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:08,658
[Matthew] Ricky!

611
00:31:08,742 --> 00:31:10,535
- Is that you?
- Yeah, hi!

612
00:31:11,078 --> 00:31:12,079
[Ricky] Looking good, man!

613
00:31:12,162 --> 00:31:13,163
[Matthew] You too!

614
00:31:13,246 --> 00:31:15,082
Ricky, I'd like you to meet...

615
00:31:16,333 --> 00:31:18,001
I'd like you to meet
my daughter, Camille.

616
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:20,962
[Ricky] Hi, nice to meet you.

617
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:22,506
Nice to meet you.

618
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:26,385
Okay, man, my table's over here.

619
00:31:26,468 --> 00:31:28,678
- Okay, see you...
- Good to see you.

620
00:31:29,679 --> 00:31:32,182
[somber music]

621
00:31:39,356 --> 00:31:41,400
[baby toy rattling]

622
00:31:47,823 --> 00:31:49,991
[cell phone ringing]

623
00:31:51,368 --> 00:31:53,328
Elisse? Hi! What's up?

624
00:31:53,954 --> 00:31:57,082
Yeah, actually,
I got Felize's stuff ready.

625
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:58,750
Yup, I gave her a bath too.

626
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:00,919
[Andrea] Oh,
and how long is the lock-in?

627
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:03,463
And why?

628
00:32:07,634 --> 00:32:08,802
Okay, just...

629
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:09,970
[exhales sharply]

630
00:32:10,053 --> 00:32:11,596
Just keep me posted, okay?

631
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:12,722
You take care.

632
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:15,183
Yeah, don't worry. I got you.

633
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:18,395
Looks like we're having a sleepover.

634
00:32:19,521 --> 00:32:20,564
Is that okay?

635
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:26,736
[cell phone ringing]

636
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:28,780
Sofie?

637
00:32:29,281 --> 00:32:30,282
Uh...

638
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:32,325
Sir Gab, were you asleep?

639
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,412
Uh, no, what's up?

640
00:32:37,664 --> 00:32:41,209
Uh, I called because
I'm really nervous about tomorrow.

641
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:42,627
I can't sleep.

642
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:47,174
I'd rather you were nervous
than complacent.

643
00:32:47,257 --> 00:32:49,342
At least now I know
you're taking this seriously.

644
00:32:50,218 --> 00:32:51,928
What if I mess up?

645
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:53,597
Take two.

646
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:55,432
What if I get up to take ten?

647
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:56,808
[chuckles]

648
00:32:57,267 --> 00:33:01,438
If you were the type to do that,
you wouldn't have gotten the part.

649
00:33:01,855 --> 00:33:04,733
[Sofie] But I hear the director
is a diva.

650
00:33:04,816 --> 00:33:07,360
Come on. That's okay.

651
00:33:08,361 --> 00:33:10,947
Besides, Chin will be there with you.

652
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:14,576
Okay. Thank you so much, Sir Gab.

653
00:33:14,826 --> 00:33:16,912
Sorry I bothered you.

654
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:18,246
- Thank you.
- Sofie.

655
00:33:18,330 --> 00:33:20,207
You did not bother me at all.

656
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,584
But you should get some sleep.
It's an early call tomorrow.

657
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:24,836
- Good night, Sir Gab. Thanks again.
- [Gab] Okay? Good night.

658
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:25,962
I'm sorry.

659
00:33:29,216 --> 00:33:30,217
[sighs]

660
00:33:38,975 --> 00:33:41,269
[line ringing]

661
00:33:41,561 --> 00:33:42,604
Hello, Chin?

662
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,316
I have an idea.

663
00:33:47,108 --> 00:33:48,401
What? Are we doing this or not?

664
00:33:48,818 --> 00:33:50,987
Get a move on! Where is my set up?

665
00:33:51,238 --> 00:33:52,739
The sun is way ahead of us, look!

666
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:55,617
Enough with the fucking coffee!

667
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:58,578
THE SOMES SIGNATURE

668
00:33:58,662 --> 00:34:00,622
[rock music]

669
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:02,874
Oh, now you're running?

670
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:04,334
Hurry up!

671
00:34:04,709 --> 00:34:05,710
What now?

672
00:34:05,794 --> 00:34:08,171
I'm Lao.
I think we're in this scene together.

673
00:34:08,588 --> 00:34:09,631
Are you alone?

674
00:34:10,090 --> 00:34:11,299
Oh, no, I have...

675
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:14,344
I have my RM with me.

676
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:16,221
Do your job, man!

677
00:34:16,304 --> 00:34:18,348
You're messing this up!

678
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:20,183
It's like dealing with kids!

679
00:34:20,267 --> 00:34:22,519
Animals! You're all stupid animals!
Nobody's moving.

680
00:34:22,602 --> 00:34:23,645
Move!

681
00:34:23,728 --> 00:34:27,148
I think we'll hear "pack up" soon.

682
00:34:27,899 --> 00:34:29,901
Oh, no, really?

683
00:34:29,985 --> 00:34:31,069
I hope not!

684
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:34,155
No more fucking questions!
Just move the darn thing!

685
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:37,075
MJ Lastimosa didn't make her flight.

686
00:34:37,701 --> 00:34:39,619
That's the second time she missed it!

687
00:34:39,703 --> 00:34:40,829
What's the problem?

688
00:34:40,912 --> 00:34:42,163
[Richard] Did you follow up on it?

689
00:34:42,247 --> 00:34:43,415
- [AD] Yes, I did.
- [Richard] Huh?

690
00:34:43,832 --> 00:34:45,834
You keep saying yes, darn you

691
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,711
but the call sheet
is a freaking mess.

692
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,087
You're a son of a gun!

693
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:51,339
You can't fool me
with those puppy dog eyes.

694
00:34:52,424 --> 00:34:54,009
Are you a freaking AD or not?

695
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:55,218
Yes, I'm an AD.

696
00:34:55,302 --> 00:34:56,678
Then why is this set all messed up?

697
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:59,055
Send everyone in that scene home!

698
00:34:59,306 --> 00:35:01,433
Now, before I trash
the freaking tent!

699
00:35:01,516 --> 00:35:02,726
- Yes, sir.
- Quickly!

700
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:05,478
- Faster!
- [AD] We're dropping a scene.

701
00:35:05,812 --> 00:35:07,897
You, you, and you. Pack up, go home.

702
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:09,899
Don't worry, you're getting paid.

703
00:35:09,983 --> 00:35:10,984
Jay.

704
00:35:11,401 --> 00:35:13,194
Take them to the field cashier.

705
00:35:13,737 --> 00:35:14,738
Now!

706
00:35:14,821 --> 00:35:16,656
[actor 1] Thank you, sir!

707
00:35:16,740 --> 00:35:18,742
[AD] Lao, pack up, you can go.

708
00:35:19,451 --> 00:35:21,494
We'll send for you again soon.

709
00:35:22,495 --> 00:35:23,747
Okay, I'm counting on it.

710
00:35:24,080 --> 00:35:25,123
Thank you!

711
00:35:25,790 --> 00:35:27,083
You're going home?

712
00:35:27,751 --> 00:35:30,253
I have a few more scenes
in this one, anyway.

713
00:35:30,337 --> 00:35:32,130
And I can hop over to another set.

714
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:33,632
Maybe there's something for me there.

715
00:35:33,715 --> 00:35:34,758
Okay!

716
00:35:35,342 --> 00:35:37,344
I'll ask Mother Aleta
for your number.

717
00:35:37,802 --> 00:35:39,220
Take care.

718
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,683
Uh, sir! What about me?

719
00:35:43,767 --> 00:35:45,810
I'm in the scene with Lao.

720
00:35:45,894 --> 00:35:47,270
But you sent him home.

721
00:35:47,354 --> 00:35:49,272
- Am I done?
- We dropped the scene.

722
00:35:50,273 --> 00:35:53,318
But I still need you, so stay. Okay?

723
00:35:53,401 --> 00:35:55,779
Okay, sir! Thank you!

724
00:35:58,365 --> 00:35:59,366
[camera shutter clicks]

725
00:36:00,200 --> 00:36:02,494
[AD] Tight shot. Close up.
Real close.

726
00:36:03,787 --> 00:36:06,539
Now step back. Take one from here.

727
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:08,166
Okay.

728
00:36:08,458 --> 00:36:09,542
There, that side.

729
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:12,128
Sofie, almost done, just a few more.

730
00:36:12,921 --> 00:36:14,214
- Good.
- [Richard] Wait!

731
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:20,220
What the heck! That blood is lousy!

732
00:36:20,595 --> 00:36:21,721
It's so fake!

733
00:36:22,055 --> 00:36:23,807
This is how it's done!

734
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:25,892
Now more! More! A lot more!

735
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:27,352
There! See that?

736
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:28,895
Now take it again!

737
00:36:29,479 --> 00:36:30,730
Need more blood! Wait!

738
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:33,233
Not enough blood for me!

739
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:34,818
Some more. Now take the shot!

740
00:36:34,901 --> 00:36:36,361
Take it!

741
00:36:37,821 --> 00:36:39,072
[AD] I told you to add more.

742
00:36:39,155 --> 00:36:42,492
Wait. More here, more more.

743
00:36:42,575 --> 00:36:44,577
Now, take it! Now that's blood!

744
00:36:44,661 --> 00:36:48,123
Now here, add more and more.

745
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:51,209
[Richard] Next set up, right away!

746
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:53,586
We're too slow. Double time!

747
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,465
- Sir!
- Hey, Gab!

748
00:36:57,549 --> 00:36:58,717
- Good afternoon.
- Nice to see you!

749
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:00,218
- You too!
- Thanks for coming.

750
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:01,845
- Sure.
- You have an actor here?

751
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:04,347
Yes, there is!
Are you done with this scene?

752
00:37:04,431 --> 00:37:05,890
- Can you check?
- [AD] Let's see.

753
00:37:06,725 --> 00:37:08,101
We dropped that scene...

754
00:37:08,393 --> 00:37:10,562
- [Gab] Ah!
- ...but we took our photos.

755
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:12,564
I see. Where's Sofie now?

756
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:13,690
She's around here somewhere.

757
00:37:13,773 --> 00:37:16,151
Okay! Director Richard,
sorry I bothered you.

758
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:17,235
I'll just look for my talent.

759
00:37:17,318 --> 00:37:18,319
- Okay, Gab.
- All right.

760
00:37:18,403 --> 00:37:19,738
What are you waiting for?

761
00:37:19,821 --> 00:37:21,781
- Set it up, faster!
- [AD] Jay, get the dolly!

762
00:37:24,868 --> 00:37:26,911
- Oh! Sir Gab!
- [Gab] Surprise!

763
00:37:26,995 --> 00:37:28,204
What are you doing here?

764
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:29,956
- [Sofie] Can't hug!
- No.

765
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:33,418
Uh, I called Chin
and told him I would come.

766
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,044
You're done for the day?

767
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:36,337
Yes, I am.

768
00:37:36,671 --> 00:37:37,672
By the way

769
00:37:37,756 --> 00:37:41,760
I've been calling Chin, but I can't
reach him because of the signal.

770
00:37:41,843 --> 00:37:42,927
Have you spoken to him?

771
00:37:43,011 --> 00:37:44,304
Looks like your visit was a waste.

772
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:45,972
Not at all!

773
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:49,476
I try to visit the set
to make sure my artists are safe.

774
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,353
Uh...

775
00:37:57,317 --> 00:37:58,568
[giggles]

776
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:00,945
Sir Gab, those guys are harmless!

777
00:38:01,029 --> 00:38:02,405
That doesn't happen in real life.

778
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:06,201
[gasps]

779
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:08,495
I'm sorry, I didn't mean it that way.

780
00:38:09,162 --> 00:38:10,705
No, it's okay.

781
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:11,956
Uh...

782
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:14,709
I'm a bit paranoid lately
because of what happened to Rob.

783
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:16,628
Um...

784
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:19,547
Anyway, back to you.

785
00:38:20,048 --> 00:38:23,343
Don't worry,
dropped scenes happen all the time.

786
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:24,677
I know.

787
00:38:24,761 --> 00:38:27,514
But it's their loss.
They didn't get to see how good I am.

788
00:38:27,597 --> 00:38:30,058
Darn straight!
But we see it all the time.

789
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:32,727
But it wasn't easy! I was over there!

790
00:38:32,811 --> 00:38:34,020
It's tough playing dead!

791
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,230
- There?
- It was something else.

792
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:36,314
Yes, right there!

793
00:38:36,940 --> 00:38:38,066
I bet you nailed it!

794
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:39,317
Of course!

795
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:43,404
Anyway, Sir Gab,
I'm going back to the office.

796
00:38:43,488 --> 00:38:44,739
Okay!

797
00:38:44,823 --> 00:38:46,366
Let's go back together.

798
00:38:47,367 --> 00:38:48,451
Um...

799
00:38:49,619 --> 00:38:51,204
You know...

800
00:38:52,038 --> 00:38:53,581
You really have an in with me.

801
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:57,001
I only visit sets
for talents who are special to me.

802
00:38:57,085 --> 00:38:59,087
[giggles]

803
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:00,380
- Don't get that on me!
- Sorry!

804
00:39:03,258 --> 00:39:04,509
[giggles]

805
00:39:04,592 --> 00:39:05,635
Thanks, bro!

806
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:07,387
He's our prosthetics guy.

807
00:39:07,470 --> 00:39:08,972
He did my gunshot here.

808
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:10,765
I can help you with that.

809
00:39:11,724 --> 00:39:13,101
JULIUS AND TINTIN
FOR THE FILIPINO FAMILY

810
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:15,228
So what's the latest news?

811
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:18,022
It's a bit sad, the rumors

812
00:39:18,106 --> 00:39:19,899
about an alleged conflict

813
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:22,110
between mother and daughter

814
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:23,778
Zsa Zsa Padilla and Karylle.

815
00:39:23,862 --> 00:39:25,363
Oh, Zsa Zsa and Karylle.

816
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:27,490
It's said that there's a disagreement

817
00:39:27,574 --> 00:39:30,034
on the direction of Karylle's career.

818
00:39:30,118 --> 00:39:32,287
But of course I understand Zsa Zsa.

819
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:35,331
We want to see our kids,
or in Zsa Zsa's case

820
00:39:35,415 --> 00:39:36,541
her daughter, succeed

821
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:38,668
or exceed what she has done.

822
00:39:38,751 --> 00:39:41,379
But does a child
really need to follow

823
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:44,757
in the footsteps
of their famous mother?

824
00:39:44,841 --> 00:39:48,052
Let's wait and see what happens next.

825
00:39:48,136 --> 00:39:49,470
JULIUS AND TINTIN
FOR THE FILIPINO FAMILY

826
00:39:51,097 --> 00:39:52,640
[Daisy gasps] Oh!

827
00:39:53,266 --> 00:39:54,309
What's all this?

828
00:39:54,726 --> 00:39:57,937
Noemi, are we
Rain Artist Management now?

829
00:39:58,021 --> 00:39:59,522
What's going on here?

830
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:02,358
No idea, and there's more of it now.

831
00:40:02,442 --> 00:40:03,860
This is Deo's fault.

832
00:40:05,653 --> 00:40:07,864
Tomorrow, I should sell

833
00:40:07,947 --> 00:40:09,616
arroz caldo and champorado.

834
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:11,451
Because it's rainy season in here!

835
00:40:12,660 --> 00:40:13,995
You're not helping, Ms. Daisy.

836
00:40:14,078 --> 00:40:16,122
This is embarrassing! We have guests!

837
00:40:16,205 --> 00:40:17,332
We're soaking our guests!

838
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:18,958
Oh, we have guests...

839
00:40:19,876 --> 00:40:22,128
[Noemi] So sorry!

840
00:40:25,006 --> 00:40:26,090
[gasps]

841
00:40:27,884 --> 00:40:28,885
Thank you.

842
00:40:30,678 --> 00:40:33,139
Where's Zsa Zsa? I thought... [gasps]

843
00:40:33,222 --> 00:40:34,557
Nothing gets past me.

844
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:37,060
Just checking for leaks.

845
00:40:38,686 --> 00:40:41,314
No leaks here.

846
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:43,358
You can shut up now, Deo.

847
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:46,152
Let's get out of here.

848
00:40:46,235 --> 00:40:47,528
Ms. Andrea has a meeting!

849
00:40:51,074 --> 00:40:52,158
[Noemi] Oh! She's here.

850
00:40:56,245 --> 00:40:57,288
Yours?

851
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:59,082
Oh! No, no.

852
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:00,792
Do you know Elisse Joson?

853
00:41:01,042 --> 00:41:02,210
This is her baby.

854
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:03,378
Of course.

855
00:41:03,461 --> 00:41:04,879
This is Felize

856
00:41:04,963 --> 00:41:07,298
I'm looking after her
while Elisse is at a shoot.

857
00:41:07,924 --> 00:41:10,051
I'm so sorry we have
to keep our voices down.

858
00:41:10,134 --> 00:41:12,345
This one is pretty hard
to put to sleep.

859
00:41:13,221 --> 00:41:14,472
I won't take long.

860
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:16,975
I just wanted to let you know that

861
00:41:17,058 --> 00:41:19,310
I've been listening
to Karylle's new songs

862
00:41:19,894 --> 00:41:23,314
and I saw her social media page.

863
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:25,858
♪ Some days we're serious ♪

864
00:41:25,942 --> 00:41:28,361
♪ Some days we laugh like this ♪

865
00:41:28,444 --> 00:41:30,530
- ♪ Some days mysterious ♪
- [Andrea] Isn't it great?

866
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:33,574
All the RMs
are working on it right now

867
00:41:33,658 --> 00:41:36,077
to get her more followers.

868
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:38,246
The songs are getting a lot of likes.

869
00:41:38,329 --> 00:41:39,914
And you know what's nice?

870
00:41:39,998 --> 00:41:42,834
We're also getting lots
of hosting gigs for her.

871
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:46,129
I saw that, and... good job.

872
00:41:46,671 --> 00:41:48,548
- Oh!
- I wanted to let you know

873
00:41:49,549 --> 00:41:51,676
that I'm very grateful
that you're giving Karylle

874
00:41:51,759 --> 00:41:55,304
the extra effort
and attention her career needs.

875
00:41:55,972 --> 00:41:57,598
Oh, that's not difficult to do.

876
00:41:57,807 --> 00:41:59,600
Karylle is so talented!

877
00:42:00,268 --> 00:42:04,230
But somehow,
I can't help but feel that...

878
00:42:05,440 --> 00:42:06,774
I'm holding her back.

879
00:42:07,692 --> 00:42:09,068
She's shutting me out.

880
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:10,945
And...

881
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:13,239
That's why

882
00:42:14,449 --> 00:42:16,117
I've decided to leave SAM.

883
00:42:17,702 --> 00:42:20,538
Wait, what? Why?

884
00:42:21,456 --> 00:42:24,125
[in Filipino] I don't want
your attention divided between us.

885
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:26,627
There's no such thing here,
Zsa Zsa, you know that.

886
00:42:26,711 --> 00:42:29,297
[in English]
I mean, we have lots of artists

887
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:31,382
but we managers do our best

888
00:42:31,466 --> 00:42:32,717
to take care of each of you.

889
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,719
You know that.
What are you talking about?

890
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:38,973
I don't want her to blame me
if something doesn't work out.

891
00:42:39,515 --> 00:42:41,851
She thinks of me as a shadow

892
00:42:42,185 --> 00:42:43,770
that she wants to escape.

893
00:42:45,605 --> 00:42:48,107
- She's your daughter.
- Exactly.

894
00:42:49,192 --> 00:42:50,777
I've already made up my mind.

895
00:42:52,028 --> 00:42:54,155
Andrea, please promise me
that you'll give her

896
00:42:54,238 --> 00:42:55,615
everything that you gave me.

897
00:42:56,032 --> 00:42:58,618
- But...
- Andrea, I have to go.

898
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:00,286
Zsa Zsa, please.

899
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:01,954
- Can we talk about this first?
- [Felize cries]

900
00:43:02,038 --> 00:43:03,247
Zsa Zsa!

901
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:05,541
[Felize wails]

902
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:09,170
Your timing, young lady,
is absolutely impeccable.

903
00:43:12,757 --> 00:43:13,925
[exhales]

904
00:43:16,135 --> 00:43:17,804
- [Chin] Ms. Andrea.
- [Andrea] Hi.

905
00:43:18,221 --> 00:43:19,472
[Chin] What happened?

906
00:43:19,555 --> 00:43:20,681
[Andrea] It's Zsa Zsa.

907
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:25,061
Never mind.

908
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,979
What's the update on Juan Makabayan?

909
00:43:27,063 --> 00:43:31,734
Um, last I heard, they were using
Bangkok for Spain.

910
00:43:32,068 --> 00:43:33,111
That's old news.

911
00:43:33,194 --> 00:43:34,570
Anything else?

912
00:43:34,654 --> 00:43:36,280
They aren't using Bangkok either.

913
00:43:36,364 --> 00:43:37,990
They might just shoot in Manila.

914
00:43:38,074 --> 00:43:40,326
That's why I can't make
the schedule work.

915
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:43,830
None of our talents are available
for the new Juan Makabayan timetable.

916
00:43:44,372 --> 00:43:46,332
We may be unable to do this project.

917
00:43:48,709 --> 00:43:50,795
Anyway, where's Camille? Is she here?

918
00:43:50,878 --> 00:43:52,046
What do you need, Ms. Andrea?

919
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:54,423
I can do it. It's Camille's turn
on the set of Portrait.

920
00:43:54,674 --> 00:43:56,551
[Andrea] Her turn?
Why are you taking turns?

921
00:43:57,301 --> 00:43:58,553
That's Maricel and Snooky together!

922
00:43:58,761 --> 00:44:01,222
If they kill each other today,
Camille can't handle that on her own!

923
00:44:01,806 --> 00:44:05,810
I was supposed to go to Sofie's shoot
but Sir Gab said he'd go.

924
00:44:06,269 --> 00:44:07,687
So what are you still doing here?

925
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:10,898
You should be at the shoot now
helping Camille out!

926
00:44:10,982 --> 00:44:14,152
If Maricel and Snooky leave us too,
then we're really screwed!

927
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:16,654
Ms. Zsa Zsa is leaving SAM?

928
00:44:18,030 --> 00:44:19,031
[scoffs]

929
00:44:19,115 --> 00:44:20,449
Ignore me.

930
00:44:20,533 --> 00:44:22,827
Just tell Camille to see me
as soon as she gets back.

931
00:44:22,910 --> 00:44:23,911
[Chin] Will do.

932
00:44:23,995 --> 00:44:26,664
What is up with this office?

933
00:44:30,209 --> 00:44:33,045
[tense music]

934
00:44:37,216 --> 00:44:40,261
[water pattering]

935
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,017
- [Matthew] Yes?
- Sir Matthew?

936
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:48,603
Just checking if you need anything.

937
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:50,563
Well, no, nothing urgent.

938
00:44:51,147 --> 00:44:54,609
But if you have time, Noemi

939
00:44:54,942 --> 00:44:55,943
read these, will you?

940
00:44:57,570 --> 00:44:59,488
There might be something good there
for our talents.

941
00:44:59,906 --> 00:45:00,948
Okay.

942
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:03,451
Oh, by the way

943
00:45:03,534 --> 00:45:05,786
Zsa Zsa is leaving SAM.

944
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:09,290
Really? Why?

945
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:11,709
She was talking to Andrea earlier.

946
00:45:12,293 --> 00:45:13,294
Just a heads up.

947
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:15,338
I'm sure Ms. Andrea
will let you know.

948
00:45:18,507 --> 00:45:19,550
I'm sure.

949
00:45:22,011 --> 00:45:23,095
I'll go.

950
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:36,192
[Paul] What you have in your hand

951
00:45:36,275 --> 00:45:38,653
is your signing bonus.

952
00:45:40,905 --> 00:45:42,740
What the heck? Hang on a second.

953
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:46,577
You said that three times already.

954
00:45:46,661 --> 00:45:48,829
Why don't you change it up?

955
00:45:50,498 --> 00:45:53,125
I'm just following the script, okay?

956
00:45:53,501 --> 00:45:55,586
[Snooky] I'm just following
the director.

957
00:45:55,670 --> 00:45:57,255
[Maricel] What are you on about?

958
00:45:57,338 --> 00:45:59,006
You're not the only actor here.

959
00:45:59,090 --> 00:46:00,383
- I am too!
- [Snooky] Oh, come on!

960
00:46:00,466 --> 00:46:01,467
Cut!

961
00:46:02,093 --> 00:46:03,094
[Maricel] Did we get it wrong?

962
00:46:03,427 --> 00:46:05,471
- No, it's all correct!
- All correct!

963
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:06,555
Yeah, but I want to stop.

964
00:46:06,639 --> 00:46:08,474
Stop? Why?

965
00:46:08,557 --> 00:46:11,519
We've been rehearsing this bit
and rehearsing some more.

966
00:46:11,602 --> 00:46:15,356
Then our co-star comes in
and changes the dialogue anyway!

967
00:46:15,439 --> 00:46:17,483
- [Chin] How are they?
- They've been at it all day.

968
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:19,485
- Huh?
- They've been at it all day.

969
00:46:19,568 --> 00:46:21,153
Screaming at each other
back and forth.

970
00:46:21,237 --> 00:46:23,948
- I need you to clear all this out.
- I think it's Sir Roderick.

971
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:27,034
[Roderick] I don't want these
distractions disrupting my acting!

972
00:46:27,118 --> 00:46:28,995
Oh, speak of the devil.

973
00:46:29,078 --> 00:46:30,329
Guys, come on! Take a look!

974
00:46:30,413 --> 00:46:32,623
- This is just a suggestion.
- [Mac] Okay...

975
00:46:32,707 --> 00:46:34,500
Wouldn't it be a better angle

976
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:36,377
- if the camera is there?
- [Mac] Where?

977
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:38,254
Here, up high over there!

978
00:46:38,337 --> 00:46:40,172
That way, when I come in...

979
00:46:40,256 --> 00:46:42,550
[playful music]

980
00:46:47,013 --> 00:46:48,389
PETRA THE HORSE
AND THE NAUGHTY KITTEN

981
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:50,391
JACK AND POY
GORIO AND TEKLA

982
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:52,226
ME AND LITTLE NINJA
SMALL AND TERRIBLE

983
00:46:52,310 --> 00:46:56,147
You know what he said?
He calls our acting old-fashioned.

984
00:46:56,230 --> 00:46:57,231
You're not offended, are you?

985
00:46:57,315 --> 00:46:58,482
Not at all!

986
00:46:58,566 --> 00:47:00,484
- For our film.
- I'll take note.

987
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:02,695
- He directs his actors?
- The nerve.

988
00:47:02,945 --> 00:47:06,574
You can't fool us, Mr. Javier!

989
00:47:07,450 --> 00:47:11,662
And you can no longer deceive us
with your lies!

990
00:47:11,746 --> 00:47:13,873
We will never believe you!

991
00:47:14,206 --> 00:47:15,207
Beautiful!

992
00:47:15,291 --> 00:47:16,292
That's it?

993
00:47:16,375 --> 00:47:17,418
[Roderick] That's all there is?

994
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,754
I'm sorry, sir, this is all wrong.

995
00:47:19,837 --> 00:47:20,880
I mean...

996
00:47:20,963 --> 00:47:21,964
Where's my script?

997
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:25,301
No, I have my own script.

998
00:47:25,384 --> 00:47:26,510
I want my script!

999
00:47:26,886 --> 00:47:28,137
My script!

1000
00:47:28,220 --> 00:47:30,097
[assistant] Here it is, sir!

1001
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:32,558
Sir, I'm not interfering here.

1002
00:47:32,641 --> 00:47:33,684
This is just a suggestion.

1003
00:47:33,768 --> 00:47:35,686
- Hang on.
- You're not intruding!

1004
00:47:35,770 --> 00:47:36,812
I know, I know!

1005
00:47:36,896 --> 00:47:39,648
So we're in the Spanish era, right?

1006
00:47:39,732 --> 00:47:42,485
Why don't we do everything
in Spanish, then?

1007
00:47:42,568 --> 00:47:44,362
Something like this. Listen.

1008
00:47:44,820 --> 00:47:46,697
[in Spanish] "No estoy engañando.

1009
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:49,909
Oh, por favor, creeme!

1010
00:47:50,534 --> 00:47:54,497
Este el unico lugar donde
de tratado de sel bueno.

1011
00:47:54,580 --> 00:47:58,000
Si sonries, no mi crees, oh!

1012
00:47:58,084 --> 00:48:00,711
Melo meresco todo bien

1013
00:48:00,795 --> 00:48:02,004
se que soy malo

1014
00:48:02,088 --> 00:48:03,631
se que soy malvado!"

1015
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,715
Something like that.

1016
00:48:04,799 --> 00:48:06,092
- You wrote that?
- Yes.

1017
00:48:06,175 --> 00:48:08,135
- [Roderick] Don't be sensitive.
- [Mac] I'm not!

1018
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:10,471
- [Roderick] Don't be mad.
- [Mac] I'm very open.

1019
00:48:10,554 --> 00:48:11,555
I'm so open to all this!

1020
00:48:11,639 --> 00:48:14,475
- I want to nail this scene!
- We're all very open.

1021
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:15,559
What's that?

1022
00:48:16,018 --> 00:48:18,062
You're lighting the scene like this?

1023
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:19,397
Perfect, huh?

1024
00:48:19,480 --> 00:48:20,481
Sir, it's too bright!

1025
00:48:20,564 --> 00:48:21,565
Bright?

1026
00:48:21,649 --> 00:48:24,610
This is a Spanish-era dungeon,
what's all this light doing in here?

1027
00:48:24,985 --> 00:48:26,278
Where's the DOP?

1028
00:48:26,654 --> 00:48:27,655
Director of Photography?

1029
00:48:28,823 --> 00:48:30,157
- Where's the DO...
- Sir?

1030
00:48:30,241 --> 00:48:31,450
Hey, young lady, where's the DOP?

1031
00:48:31,534 --> 00:48:32,910
- She is the DOP!
- I'm the DOP.

1032
00:48:32,993 --> 00:48:34,453
Are you? Sorry!

1033
00:48:35,496 --> 00:48:36,664
See that light over there?

1034
00:48:36,956 --> 00:48:39,125
It's too bright.
It's like there's a moon in here.

1035
00:48:39,917 --> 00:48:40,918
How about you kill it?

1036
00:48:41,293 --> 00:48:43,671
Joven, kill this one.

1037
00:48:44,088 --> 00:48:46,132
- [Roderick] There!
- [Mac] Better!

1038
00:48:46,465 --> 00:48:48,217
- Now it's perfect?
- Yeah, hang on.

1039
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:49,427
Sir, another suggestion.

1040
00:48:49,510 --> 00:48:51,011
It's still a bit too bright.

1041
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:52,346
How about we kill this one too?

1042
00:48:52,680 --> 00:48:54,181
- Kill it.
- [Mac] Kill it.

1043
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:55,391
Kill it.

1044
00:48:56,767 --> 00:48:57,935
- Yes!
- Okay...

1045
00:48:58,018 --> 00:48:59,728
- One more, sir...
- One more?

1046
00:48:59,812 --> 00:49:01,814
This one is still too bright.

1047
00:49:02,064 --> 00:49:03,524
For balance, kill this one too.

1048
00:49:03,607 --> 00:49:04,608
Kill it.

1049
00:49:04,692 --> 00:49:06,902
- [Roderick] That's it!
- [Mac] Okay... Happy now?

1050
00:49:06,986 --> 00:49:08,571
- Happy.
- [Roderick] Hey, my eyes!

1051
00:49:08,654 --> 00:49:09,738
What is that?

1052
00:49:09,822 --> 00:49:10,948
- A spotlight.
- Sir.

1053
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:12,032
- Top light.
- Hear me out.

1054
00:49:12,116 --> 00:49:13,117
Is that fluorescent lighting?

1055
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:14,869
Fluorescent lights didn't exist then.

1056
00:49:15,244 --> 00:49:17,204
- Turn it off!
- Turn it off, now.

1057
00:49:17,288 --> 00:49:19,707
Get rid of this one too.

1058
00:49:20,583 --> 00:49:22,751
- [Roderick] There!
- [Mac] That's it!

1059
00:49:22,835 --> 00:49:24,044
[Roderick] Perfecto!

1060
00:49:24,128 --> 00:49:25,546
[Mac] You're the best!

1061
00:49:25,629 --> 00:49:27,006
You're the Dick!

1062
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:29,467
Let's do a take! Thank you, Dick!

1063
00:49:29,550 --> 00:49:32,261
Utility! Coffee! Boiling hot!

1064
00:49:32,845 --> 00:49:34,513
[Roderick] Sir,
these are just suggestions...

1065
00:49:36,056 --> 00:49:37,475
Small suggestions!

1066
00:49:37,558 --> 00:49:40,186
He's so full of himself
like he's everything!

1067
00:49:40,269 --> 00:49:41,312
Well, wow!

1068
00:49:42,146 --> 00:49:43,189
Just like you!

1069
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:46,066
Me? How am I like him?

1070
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:48,527
Poor you.

1071
00:49:48,611 --> 00:49:49,820
Having to deal with this drama.

1072
00:49:49,904 --> 00:49:51,280
This is too much for anyone.

1073
00:49:51,864 --> 00:49:53,574
You should go back to the office.

1074
00:49:53,657 --> 00:49:55,618
Ms. Andrea is looking for you anyway.

1075
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:57,745
- Thank you.
- I'll take care of things here.

1076
00:49:57,828 --> 00:50:00,956
Miss Maricel? Miss Snooky? I'm going.

1077
00:50:01,040 --> 00:50:02,208
You're leaving?

1078
00:50:03,626 --> 00:50:05,461
I might as well leave. Let's go.

1079
00:50:06,670 --> 00:50:08,422
#JUSTSHARINGSIS

1080
00:50:08,506 --> 00:50:10,216
Hello to my subscribers!

1081
00:50:10,299 --> 00:50:13,135
Do you remember the tea last time

1082
00:50:13,219 --> 00:50:14,803
about that problematic project

1083
00:50:14,887 --> 00:50:17,765
of indie director Lav Diaz

1084
00:50:17,848 --> 00:50:21,810
and veteran action star
Monsour del Rosario.

1085
00:50:22,728 --> 00:50:26,524
Reports say that their film
can't reach the finish line.

1086
00:50:26,607 --> 00:50:27,983
People are stressed.

1087
00:50:28,067 --> 00:50:29,693
Some shooting days got wasted.

1088
00:50:29,777 --> 00:50:31,779
A lot of back and forth conflicts.

1089
00:50:31,862 --> 00:50:35,241
The two can't agree on their vision.

1090
00:50:35,324 --> 00:50:37,701
Creative differences, so to speak.

1091
00:50:39,161 --> 00:50:42,206
Rumor has it that they're both ready
to just shelve the whole thing

1092
00:50:42,289 --> 00:50:43,666
and forget anything happened.

1093
00:50:43,749 --> 00:50:44,875
What a shame, right?

1094
00:50:44,959 --> 00:50:46,335
#JUSTSHARINGSIS

1095
00:50:50,422 --> 00:50:53,926
[Gab] Hey,
are these leaks increasing?

1096
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,636
- Hey.
- [Sofie] What's happening?

1097
00:50:55,844 --> 00:50:57,054
What a mess!

1098
00:50:57,471 --> 00:50:59,265
- [Gab] There are way more leaks now!
- Oh, no.

1099
00:50:59,348 --> 00:51:01,934
It's even worse in the rooms.

1100
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:04,895
We brought snacks. Where's Andrea?

1101
00:51:05,437 --> 00:51:06,689
Maybe by the swing.

1102
00:51:07,022 --> 00:51:08,857
Sofie, can we switch now?

1103
00:51:08,941 --> 00:51:10,025
- I have work to do.
- Of course!

1104
00:51:10,109 --> 00:51:11,277
- Thank you, Sir Gab!
- Okay!

1105
00:51:13,487 --> 00:51:15,322
[Noemi] Oh, Sir Gab, wait!

1106
00:51:15,614 --> 00:51:16,657
Why?

1107
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:20,494
Be careful.

1108
00:51:20,578 --> 00:51:21,620
Careful? Why?

1109
00:51:22,496 --> 00:51:23,622
Zsa Zsa is leaving us.

1110
00:51:24,665 --> 00:51:25,666
Ah.

1111
00:51:26,458 --> 00:51:27,501
Thank you.

1112
00:51:29,211 --> 00:51:30,796
[Noemi] Is that sans rival?

1113
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:33,048
Come on, let's eat!

1114
00:51:33,799 --> 00:51:35,759
Yeah, but I'm on a diet.

1115
00:51:36,844 --> 00:51:38,470
- Really now?
- But thank you!

1116
00:51:38,554 --> 00:51:39,930
Hey, don't I get a bite?

1117
00:51:40,014 --> 00:51:41,348
Sir Gab said this was all mine!

1118
00:51:41,432 --> 00:51:42,600
You know, you're too much!

1119
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:45,644
He kept you company the whole day
and now you want his food too?

1120
00:51:48,022 --> 00:51:49,356
I hope you get diarrhea.

1121
00:51:51,442 --> 00:51:53,819
[Gab] What a cute baby!
Give me a kiss.

1122
00:51:53,902 --> 00:51:54,903
[Andrea] Hey, quit that!

1123
00:51:55,654 --> 00:51:58,157
You're gonna give her rashes!

1124
00:51:58,240 --> 00:52:01,243
Baby, monster. What a meanie!

1125
00:52:01,327 --> 00:52:03,329
Facial hair is dirty, okay?

1126
00:52:03,412 --> 00:52:04,496
Oh, come on.

1127
00:52:05,831 --> 00:52:07,082
What are you doing here?

1128
00:52:07,499 --> 00:52:09,251
She doesn't like the swing,
so I'm playing with her.

1129
00:52:14,548 --> 00:52:16,133
I hear Zsa Zsa is leaving?

1130
00:52:16,425 --> 00:52:17,926
[Andrea] How did you know?

1131
00:52:19,053 --> 00:52:20,054
[clicks tongue]

1132
00:52:20,596 --> 00:52:21,597
Oh, dear.

1133
00:52:23,390 --> 00:52:26,226
Aside from that thing with Zsa Zsa

1134
00:52:28,062 --> 00:52:29,688
if we don't find out

1135
00:52:30,272 --> 00:52:33,942
who's leaking our office secrets.

1136
00:52:35,110 --> 00:52:37,696
Brandon and Jessica might leave too!

1137
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:43,452
Plus this Monsour movie,
with no end in sight.

1138
00:52:43,535 --> 00:52:46,372
With all the stunts Lav made him do.

1139
00:52:47,081 --> 00:52:48,082
It's never-ending.

1140
00:52:48,499 --> 00:52:50,459
There's no end to this chaos.

1141
00:52:50,793 --> 00:52:53,671
At least Rob is all better now.

1142
00:52:54,171 --> 00:52:56,924
But we can't even protect the kid
against Frank Villacin.

1143
00:52:59,134 --> 00:53:00,135
And SAM...

1144
00:53:02,721 --> 00:53:06,392
We may never be able to buy it!

1145
00:53:07,726 --> 00:53:11,021
You can't get a decent answer
out of Matthew.

1146
00:53:11,105 --> 00:53:13,065
It's all, "I'll take care of it."

1147
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:14,191
You know how this will end?

1148
00:53:14,274 --> 00:53:17,653
We lose not just the artists,
but the entire agency.

1149
00:53:19,780 --> 00:53:20,781
[sighs]

1150
00:53:21,824 --> 00:53:24,785
Anyway, Elisse called.

1151
00:53:25,869 --> 00:53:27,496
She's taking the baby home.

1152
00:53:28,330 --> 00:53:29,331
Well...

1153
00:53:29,873 --> 00:53:31,625
that's good news, right?

1154
00:53:33,877 --> 00:53:37,297
You know, Rina and I talked once.

1155
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:41,093
About adopting a baby.

1156
00:53:41,885 --> 00:53:42,970
She always wanted a baby.

1157
00:53:43,262 --> 00:53:44,263
Me, not so much.

1158
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:46,849
But now you do?

1159
00:53:48,517 --> 00:53:49,518
Well...

1160
00:53:50,561 --> 00:53:51,854
People change, you know.

1161
00:53:52,563 --> 00:53:54,022
Then have a baby.

1162
00:53:56,358 --> 00:53:59,528
I don't think I can have babies
with the people I'm dating now.

1163
00:53:59,611 --> 00:54:01,196
I mean, they're not Rina.

1164
00:54:01,905 --> 00:54:05,701
You don't need Rina
or anybody to have a baby.

1165
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:07,327
Just do it!

1166
00:54:08,328 --> 00:54:09,788
[Gab] There are many ways
to have a baby.

1167
00:54:09,872 --> 00:54:11,665
No need to borrow someone else's.

1168
00:54:12,833 --> 00:54:15,043
- [babbles]
- [cell phone ringing]

1169
00:54:15,127 --> 00:54:16,253
Mommy's calling!

1170
00:54:18,130 --> 00:54:19,631
Hi, Elisse!

1171
00:54:19,923 --> 00:54:22,092
How are you? Are you done shooting?

1172
00:54:22,176 --> 00:54:25,345
Don't worry about Felize.
She's still with me.

1173
00:54:25,429 --> 00:54:28,265
And if you need me to still babysit,
I can do it!

1174
00:54:28,348 --> 00:54:29,475
- Are you okay?
- [Elisse] Oh, no.

1175
00:54:29,558 --> 00:54:31,894
Actually, I'm at your door. I'm here.

1176
00:54:31,977 --> 00:54:34,021
- Yes, yes!
- [Andrea] Okay.

1177
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:39,610
- [Elisse] Andrea.
- You wrapped early today!

1178
00:54:39,693 --> 00:54:40,944
Great, isn't it? Thank you so much!

1179
00:54:41,028 --> 00:54:42,446
- Hi, baby!
- [Andrea] Come in!

1180
00:54:42,529 --> 00:54:44,114
[Elisse] Oh, here's her stuff.

1181
00:54:44,198 --> 00:54:46,575
So sorry, I'm in a rush.

1182
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:48,243
Oh, no worries.

1183
00:54:48,577 --> 00:54:50,454
Um... When is your next shoot?

1184
00:54:51,163 --> 00:54:52,164
Um...

1185
00:54:52,247 --> 00:54:54,208
- I don't know yet.
- Joseph?

1186
00:54:54,291 --> 00:54:55,709
- Can someone help me?
- Of course!

1187
00:54:55,793 --> 00:54:57,544
Joseph, help Elisse with her things.

1188
00:54:57,628 --> 00:54:59,213
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you!

1189
00:54:59,296 --> 00:55:00,380
Um...

1190
00:55:00,464 --> 00:55:03,550
If you have another shoot,
I'll be here, you know that.

1191
00:55:03,634 --> 00:55:04,676
Thank you so much.

1192
00:55:04,760 --> 00:55:06,970
But it's all good.
Felize's nanny is back home with me.

1193
00:55:07,054 --> 00:55:08,180
- Oh, okay.
- Hey, baby.

1194
00:55:08,931 --> 00:55:10,390
- Okay.
- Mommy's here!

1195
00:55:10,474 --> 00:55:11,725
Thank you, I owe you one!

1196
00:55:11,809 --> 00:55:13,727
- No worries.
- Say bye-bye!

1197
00:55:13,811 --> 00:55:14,895
- Bye-bye!
- Bye!

1198
00:55:14,978 --> 00:55:16,021
Thank you!

1199
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:17,981
Let's go!

1200
00:55:18,482 --> 00:55:20,734
Hey, Elisse?

1201
00:55:22,194 --> 00:55:24,196
[dramatic music]

1202
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:40,712
The bruises on his face are healing

1203
00:55:40,796 --> 00:55:43,382
after the beating that Rob Gomez got.

1204
00:55:43,465 --> 00:55:45,133
Good thing he's recovering quickly.

1205
00:55:45,217 --> 00:55:48,637
Or else,
I'd be better-looking than him.

1206
00:55:48,720 --> 00:55:50,180
According to my source

1207
00:55:50,264 --> 00:55:53,767
Rob's body took a heavy beating

1208
00:55:53,851 --> 00:55:56,311
including his business down there.

1209
00:55:56,395 --> 00:55:58,021
Scary! The question is

1210
00:55:58,105 --> 00:56:00,524
who would do such a thing to Rob?

1211
00:56:00,607 --> 00:56:02,985
I know, and I'm sure you do too.

1212
00:56:03,068 --> 00:56:04,361
I'll leave it up to you to decide

1213
00:56:04,444 --> 00:56:09,533
who this vindictive figure is.

1214
00:56:09,616 --> 00:56:10,701
And of course

1215
00:56:10,784 --> 00:56:14,371
what did Rob do to deserve this?

1216
00:56:14,454 --> 00:56:16,039
Is a woman involved?

1217
00:56:16,123 --> 00:56:17,165
[Mr. Fu] I have the answers.

1218
00:56:17,249 --> 00:56:20,711
But do I want to share them?

1219
00:56:20,794 --> 00:56:21,920
Keep buzzin'!

1220
00:56:23,839 --> 00:56:25,048
[Matthew] That's a lot of pictures.

1221
00:56:25,799 --> 00:56:27,885
There were some fans
who took pictures with him

1222
00:56:27,968 --> 00:56:29,136
at the hospital.

1223
00:56:29,595 --> 00:56:33,223
I mean, he still looked great,
despite the bruises.

1224
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:34,933
Chin, you should've stopped them.

1225
00:56:35,017 --> 00:56:36,685
I did my best, Ms. Andrea.

1226
00:56:36,768 --> 00:56:38,270
I mean, I got him out
of there safely.

1227
00:56:38,979 --> 00:56:40,981
The marks on his face are visible.

1228
00:56:41,064 --> 00:56:42,566
Yes, we know that.

1229
00:56:43,150 --> 00:56:46,278
The pictures aren't the problem.
We all go to the hospital, right?

1230
00:56:47,154 --> 00:56:49,531
But the details about his beating?

1231
00:56:50,324 --> 00:56:51,325
Matty?

1232
00:56:51,950 --> 00:56:53,201
Could it have been your niece?

1233
00:56:53,285 --> 00:56:54,786
- [Matthew] Rachel?
- [Andrea] Yeah?

1234
00:56:54,870 --> 00:56:56,121
No, not possible.

1235
00:56:56,622 --> 00:56:58,123
She's always been very discreet.

1236
00:56:58,206 --> 00:56:59,875
Besides, she doesn't even know Rob.

1237
00:57:00,500 --> 00:57:02,711
She doesn't care for show business.

1238
00:57:02,794 --> 00:57:05,380
[Chin] And when Rob left
the examination room

1239
00:57:05,464 --> 00:57:06,465
she stayed behind.

1240
00:57:06,548 --> 00:57:08,258
She couldn't have taken the pictures.

1241
00:57:08,342 --> 00:57:09,718
So where are those from?

1242
00:57:09,801 --> 00:57:10,928
Poor Rob.

1243
00:57:25,776 --> 00:57:28,695
[Deo] If I'm being completely honest,
ma'am, sirs...

1244
00:57:28,779 --> 00:57:29,780
Uh...

1245
00:57:29,863 --> 00:57:32,032
I don't know any of your actors here.

1246
00:57:32,115 --> 00:57:33,825
I'm not interested in them.

1247
00:57:33,909 --> 00:57:36,036
I only know two.

1248
00:57:36,620 --> 00:57:37,788
My idol Monsour

1249
00:57:37,871 --> 00:57:40,082
and Brandon, only if he wins fights.

1250
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:43,585
I don't even remember
his wife's name.

1251
00:57:43,669 --> 00:57:45,504
So I really don't know this...

1252
00:57:45,879 --> 00:57:47,422
Rod Golez?

1253
00:57:49,049 --> 00:57:50,050
Rob Gomez.

1254
00:57:51,093 --> 00:57:53,637
While we were talking here,
you were by the door.

1255
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:54,721
Were you eavesdropping?

1256
00:57:55,973 --> 00:57:57,808
- No.
- Then why were you there?

1257
00:57:57,891 --> 00:58:00,978
I was waiting for you to finish.
I left the vacuum cleaner in here.

1258
00:58:08,735 --> 00:58:09,736
Well, okay then.

1259
00:58:10,612 --> 00:58:11,655
Take it.

1260
00:58:15,867 --> 00:58:17,369
[Andrea] Daisy,
we're not done with you.

1261
00:58:17,953 --> 00:58:19,454
- Sit down.
- Oh, no.

1262
00:58:19,955 --> 00:58:21,915
Ma'am, I swear I didn't do this.

1263
00:58:21,999 --> 00:58:23,291
I know nothing.

1264
00:58:23,625 --> 00:58:25,377
But you know Cristy Fermin?

1265
00:58:26,920 --> 00:58:28,505
Of course I do.

1266
00:58:28,588 --> 00:58:31,508
But we're not close.
I don't know her in person.

1267
00:58:31,800 --> 00:58:33,010
You didn't message her?

1268
00:58:33,093 --> 00:58:35,387
Oh, no, Sir Gab.

1269
00:58:35,470 --> 00:58:37,681
I know absolutely nothing about this.

1270
00:58:37,764 --> 00:58:39,433
I would never do that to Rob.

1271
00:58:39,516 --> 00:58:41,476
[Daisy] He is so kind to me.

1272
00:58:41,560 --> 00:58:44,062
And I don't care for tea like that.

1273
00:58:44,146 --> 00:58:45,272
It's too scary!

1274
00:58:45,355 --> 00:58:47,691
I only remember one rumor I spread.

1275
00:58:47,774 --> 00:58:49,860
About Sir Samuel's cause of death.

1276
00:58:49,943 --> 00:58:54,865
Now if you don't believe me,
then I'm going to resign.

1277
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:57,534
Daisy, you can't resign.

1278
00:58:57,826 --> 00:58:59,995
But you don't trust me anymore!

1279
00:59:00,078 --> 00:59:03,665
You can't resign
because you don't work here.

1280
00:59:06,877 --> 00:59:10,213
Ms. Andrea, Sir Matt, Sir Gab.

1281
00:59:10,297 --> 00:59:12,049
I really know nothing about this.

1282
00:59:12,132 --> 00:59:13,842
It wasn't me.

1283
00:59:14,176 --> 00:59:16,553
I don't know why, but I believe you.

1284
00:59:18,055 --> 00:59:19,431
Don't be mad at us.

1285
00:59:19,723 --> 00:59:21,725
We just really need to do this.

1286
00:59:23,143 --> 00:59:25,312
You can go, Daisy, thank you.

1287
00:59:27,230 --> 00:59:28,315
Thank you!

1288
00:59:35,489 --> 00:59:37,115
[Daisy gasps]

1289
00:59:37,365 --> 00:59:38,366
Excuse me.

1290
00:59:41,995 --> 00:59:43,121
It's not them.

1291
00:59:45,415 --> 00:59:46,416
Agree.

1292
00:59:48,794 --> 00:59:50,462
But you know what this means, right?

1293
00:59:53,090 --> 00:59:54,716
It could be any one of us.

1294
00:59:56,051 --> 00:59:58,053
[somber music]

1295
01:00:00,847 --> 01:00:02,265
Favorite quote?

1296
01:00:03,225 --> 01:00:04,768
"This too shall pass."

1297
01:00:05,644 --> 01:00:08,313
The popular
are never popular for life.

1298
01:00:09,314 --> 01:00:10,357
The nobodies

1299
01:00:11,108 --> 01:00:12,943
won't always be nobodies.

1300
01:00:14,111 --> 01:00:15,570
"This too shall pass."

1301
01:00:16,113 --> 01:00:18,490
That's what I always tell myself

1302
01:00:19,116 --> 01:00:20,534
to keep me on my toes.

1303
01:00:21,243 --> 01:00:22,452
To keep me alert.

1304
01:00:23,745 --> 01:00:25,122
WHAT'S THE TEA?
WITH OGIE DIAZ

1305
01:00:25,205 --> 01:00:30,043
The biggest talent agency here

1306
01:00:30,127 --> 01:00:32,712
is Shine Artist Management.

1307
01:00:32,796 --> 01:00:35,674
But talk is, it's about to close!

1308
01:00:35,757 --> 01:00:37,676
According to rumors

1309
01:00:37,759 --> 01:00:41,638
the company will have
new management soon.

1310
01:00:41,721 --> 01:00:44,141
Someone wants to take over.

1311
01:00:44,224 --> 01:00:46,852
This person is Very Famous.

1312
01:00:46,935 --> 01:00:48,854
And get this.

1313
01:00:48,937 --> 01:00:51,273
Another one, an Affluent Producer

1314
01:00:51,356 --> 01:00:54,860
also wants the company.

1315
01:00:54,943 --> 01:00:57,737
[Ogie] But all this talk
about business...

1316
01:00:57,821 --> 01:00:59,614
What? It's not me!

1317
01:00:59,698 --> 01:01:00,991
Nothing!

1318
01:01:01,074 --> 01:01:05,036
Here's what I'm worried about...

1319
01:01:06,163 --> 01:01:08,165
[line ringing]

1320
01:01:10,959 --> 01:01:12,002
Andrea?

1321
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:14,337
[Andrea] Why is this in the news?

1322
01:01:16,840 --> 01:01:18,884
I said it was too early to announce!

1323
01:01:22,387 --> 01:01:25,056
Do you think they meant us
when they said "new management"?

1324
01:01:25,932 --> 01:01:28,143
Helen hasn't even accepted our offer.

1325
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:31,813
[Matthew] And where do I get
the money to pay for that?

1326
01:01:33,023 --> 01:01:34,149
Go back to Gina.

1327
01:01:38,403 --> 01:01:39,529
Andrea...

1328
01:01:42,699 --> 01:01:43,950
I tried that before.

1329
01:01:46,953 --> 01:01:48,288
She doesn't even want to see me.

1330
01:01:49,331 --> 01:01:51,541
What if you get a loan from Brandon?

1331
01:01:53,126 --> 01:01:54,502
[Matthew] Are you crazy?
That's too risky.

1332
01:01:55,462 --> 01:01:57,255
We'll lose any leverage
we still have.

1333
01:01:58,215 --> 01:02:01,551
If this goes south one day
and we can't pay him back

1334
01:02:02,344 --> 01:02:03,637
he could end up owning SAM.

1335
01:02:06,056 --> 01:02:08,934
Okay, scratch Brandon.

1336
01:02:09,017 --> 01:02:10,894
Banks. What about banks?

1337
01:02:10,977 --> 01:02:11,978
Maybe.

1338
01:02:12,062 --> 01:02:13,188
I mean, we're viable.

1339
01:02:13,730 --> 01:02:15,482
Maybe with a solid business plan...

1340
01:02:17,776 --> 01:02:18,818
Wait.

1341
01:02:20,987 --> 01:02:23,698
Closing shop or new management.

1342
01:02:24,532 --> 01:02:26,034
[Andrea] What if those two
are the same thing?

1343
01:02:26,451 --> 01:02:27,494
Huh?

1344
01:02:28,245 --> 01:02:29,496
What are you talking about?

1345
01:02:30,080 --> 01:02:31,122
How does that work?

1346
01:02:31,206 --> 01:02:32,332
[Andrea] Affluent Producer.

1347
01:02:33,333 --> 01:02:34,376
Or AP.

1348
01:02:35,919 --> 01:02:36,962
Amir Paul!

1349
01:02:37,212 --> 01:02:38,421
What if...

1350
01:02:40,173 --> 01:02:43,843
Paul Amir is the new management
who will close SAM down?

1351
01:02:44,261 --> 01:02:45,262
Hm?

1352
01:02:45,345 --> 01:02:46,680
I'm thinking of something far worse.

1353
01:02:48,807 --> 01:02:50,225
[Matthew] Very Famous.

1354
01:02:50,308 --> 01:02:51,601
SAM'S NEW OWNER?

1355
01:02:51,685 --> 01:02:53,061
VF.

1356
01:02:53,770 --> 01:02:54,813
[Gab] VF.

1357
01:02:55,397 --> 01:02:56,398
V...

1358
01:02:56,481 --> 01:02:57,524
Shoot.

1359
01:02:58,733 --> 01:03:00,193
- Frank Villacin!
- [Andrea] Frank Villacin!

1360
01:03:00,277 --> 01:03:03,738
SAM'S NEW OWNER?
FRANK VILLACIN

1361
01:03:04,239 --> 01:03:05,573
Shoot.

1362
01:03:06,157 --> 01:03:07,617
Here's what I'm worried about.

1363
01:03:08,076 --> 01:03:12,998
Are their talents aware
of these rumored movements?

1364
01:03:13,623 --> 01:03:16,042
It's going to be chaos.

1365
01:03:16,126 --> 01:03:18,545
[Ogie] Do they know what's happening?

1366
01:03:19,921 --> 01:03:21,715
Does it matter to regular fans?

1367
01:03:21,798 --> 01:03:22,841
Not really.

1368
01:03:24,467 --> 01:03:27,679
Let's see what happens.

1369
01:03:27,762 --> 01:03:31,683
Hold on, let me call somebody.

1370
01:03:31,766 --> 01:03:34,144
[ominous music]

1371
01:03:34,227 --> 01:03:36,271
To get the latest updates.

1372
01:03:36,354 --> 01:03:37,689
[Ogie laughs]

1373
01:03:38,064 --> 01:03:41,067
[loud crash]

1374
01:03:41,401 --> 01:03:43,945
[water trickling]

1375
01:03:48,325 --> 01:03:50,327
[closing theme music]
